<p>Joyce Appleby, ed., <em>Recollections of the Early Republic: Selected Autobiographies</em> (1997); Daniel Walker Howe, <em>What Hath God Wrought: The Transformation of America, 1815–1848</em> (2007); Charles Sellers, <em>The Market Revolution: Jacksonian America, 1815–1846</em> (1991); Carol Sheriff, <em>The Artificial River: The Erie Canal and the Paradox of Progress, 1817-1862</em> (1996); Harry L. Watson, <em>Liberty and Power: The Politics of Jacksonian America</em> (1990); Peter Way, <em>Common Labour: Workers and the Digging of North American Canals, 1780–1860</em> (1993); and Sean Wilentz, <em>The Rise of American Democracy: Jefferson to Lincoln </em>(2005).
</p>


